2] \"Well.\" said the Earl of Carringham. \"Then it's settled. Old chap, I am very glad, very happy.\" [2413] He forced a cheerful attitude and whispered to Mr. Fitch that he had to find the constable, and then escaped from the room. [2414] In the living room, he saw Virginia walking down the stairs. [2415] \"Would you like me to accompany you for breakfast?\" asked the Earl of Carringham gently. [2416] \"I've already eaten in bed, thank you. I'm just so tired this morning,\" she yawned. [2417] \"Didn't sleep well?\" [2418] \"Not really, actually slept quite well, Lord Carrington,\" she slipped her hand into his arm and held on tightly, \"I'm having a wonderful time here, it's so kind of you to have me, dear.\" [2419] \"Then stay a few more days, won't you? Constable Batterton lifted the ban, but I'd really like you to stay. So would Bunder.\" [2420] \"Of course, that's very thoughtful of you.\" [2421] \"Hmm!\" Lord Caterham said. [2422] He sighed. [2423] \"Do you have something you can't tell me?\" Virginia asked, \"Did someone bite you?\" [2424] \"Exactly.\" Lord Caterham said mournfully. [2425] Virginia looked perplexed. [2426] \"You're not going to kick me, are you? I know you wouldn't. Never mind, it doesn't matter.\" [2427] The Earl of Carringham sadly walked away, and Virginia went through the side door into the garden. [2428] She stood there for a moment, breathing in the fresh air. The October air felt invigorating to her slightly tired body. [2429] She jumped, startled, as she suddenly realized that Constable Bartle was standing right beside her. This man seemed to have a knack for appearing out of nowhere. [2430] \"Good morning, Mrs. Rue. How are you feeling? Not too tired, I hope?\" [2431] Virginia shook her head. [2432] \"It was quite an exciting night,\" she said. \"It's worth sacrificing some sleep, the only regret is that today seems a bit boring.\" [2433] \"There's a shady spot under that pine tree,\" said Chief Batter. \"I'll bring you a chair there?\" [2434] \"It's fine if you think it's fine,\" said Virginia seriously. [2435] \"You're sharp, Mrs. Rue. That's the truth, and I want to talk to you.\" [2436] He brought a wicker chair out onto the lawn, and Virginia followed with a cushion under her arm. [2437] \"The platform is too dangerous,\" Bates said. \"I mean, if we want to talk privately.\" [2438] \"I'm getting excited again, Chief Bates.\" [2439] \"Nothing important,\" he said, pulling out a large pocket watch and glancing at it. \"Ten thirty, I still have ten minutes before I go to Wivenhoe Abbey to report to Mr. Romax. I just want to hear more about Mr. Kidd.\" [2440] \"Mr. Kidd?\" Virginia was surprised. [2441] \"Well, for instance, where did you meet, and how long have you known each other.\" [2442] Detective Batter acted cool and friendly, not even looking at her. But the more he did that, the more Virginia felt uneasy. [2443] \"It's not as simple as you think,\" she said at last. \"He did me a big favor once\u2014\"\n[2444] Batter interrupted her. [2445] \"Mrs. Rue, I'll interrupt. Last night, after you and Mr. Everly retired to your room, Mr. Kidd told me all about the letters and the murdered man at your house.\" [2446] \"He told you?\" Virginia held her breath. [2447] \"Yes, it was wise to clarify things. There's just one thing he didn't tell me, and that's how long you've known each other. I have an idea about that, and I just need to know if I'm right. The day he went to your house on Pound Street was your first meeting. I was right, wasn't I?\" [2448] Virginia didn't speak. For the first time, this expressionless, slow-witted person made her feel afraid. She finally understood why Anthony said Sheriff Barton was very sharp. [2449] \"Has he told you about his life before South Africa?\" Barton continued. \"I mean, in Canada, or before that, in Sudan, or even his childhood?\" [2450] Virginia just shook her head. [2451] \"I'll bet he's a man with a story to tell. It's written all over his face,