all.\" [2473] \"Excellent. Good morning, Mr. Everly.\" [2474] \"Shall we take a walk together?\" the Frenchman suggested. [2475] \"What do you think, Bill?\" Virginia asked. [2476] \"Alright.\" Bill answered reluctantly. [2477] Bill got up from the grass and the three of them strolled along slowly. Virginia walked in between them, and immediately sensed a strange excitement in the Frenchman's heart, but she had no idea what it was about. [2478] Soon, she managed to relax him using her usual techniques by asking questions, listening, and gradually leading him to talk about his interests. He began to tell interesting stories about the famous King Victor, despite his resentment in the tone of voice when talking about how King Victor tricked the police department. [2479] Although Leon was fully engaged in telling the story, Virginia always felt that he had something else on his mind. [2480] Moreover, she noticed that under the guise of telling stories, Leon was secretly plotting a path through the courtyard. They weren't just strolling; he was deliberately leading them in a certain direction. [2481] Suddenly, the story stopped, and he looked around. [2482] At that moment, they were standing in the middle of the courtyard, with a sharp turn just ahead by the bushes. Lemont was staring intently at a car approaching from the direction of the villa. [2483] Virginia followed his gaze. [2484] \"That's the luggage car,\" she said. \"It's taking the luggage and the valet to the train station in Azerbaijan.\" [2485] \"Is it?\" Lemont said, glancing at his watch. \"I'm sorry, I didn't realize I stayed so long. Would it be okay if I hitched a ride with them to the village?\" [2486] LeMont walked down the driveway, raising his arm to signal, and the luggage car stopped. He explained a few words, and then climbed up from the back. He politely tipped his hat to Virginia and drove off. [2487] The other two watched the car drive away, puzzled. Just as the car turned the corner, a suitcase fell onto the driveway, but the car didn't stop. [2488] \"Come on,\" Virginia said to Bill. \"Something interesting is happening. The suitcase was thrown out.\" [2489] \"It's amazing it wasn't noticed,\" Bill said. They ran down the driveway to the suitcase. Just as they were about to get to the suitcase, LeMont came around the corner, panting slightly from the quick walk. [2490] \"I had to get out,\" he said cheerfully. \"I realized I left something behind.\" [2491] \"This one?\" Bill asked, pointing to the suitcase. [2492] It was a very nice thick leather box with \"H.I.\" abbreviated on it. [2493] \"Too bad,\" Remy whispered. \"It must have fallen out, we should move it from the middle of the road, right?\" [2494] Before the two could answer, he picked up the box and moved it to the side of the row of trees. He bent down and something flashed in his hand, and the lock of the box was opened. [2495] He spoke a sentence, but his voice was different from before, fast and commanding:\n[2496] \"The car will be here soon,\" he said. \"Is it here yet?\" [2497] Virginia turned around to look at the villa. [2498] \"No.\" [2499] \"Good.\" [2500] He quickly took out the contents of the box one by one: bottles with gold lids, silk pajamas, various socks. Suddenly, he stiffened. He grabbed a package that looked like silk lingerie and quickly opened it. [2501] Bill couldn't help but let out a soft \"Oh\" as he saw a heavy-looking handgun in the center of the package. [2502] \"I hear the horn,\" Virginia said. [2503] Lemon quickly organized the suitcase, wrapped the gun in his silk handkerchief, and put it in his pocket. Then he locked the suitcase with a \"click\" and turned to Bill:\n[2504] \"Take this, you and the lady. Stop the car and tell them the suitcase fell out of the luggage compartment. Don't mention me.\" [2505] Bill quickly walked down the driveway as the Lancaster sedan approached the turn, with Eisakstein inside. The driver slowed down, and Bill waved the suitcase at him. [2506] \"This suitcase fell out of the trunk,\" he explained, \"We just happened to see it.\" [2507] He saw the financier's yellow face go blank, staring at him intently. Then, the car continued on its way. [2508] They turned around and found Lemmon standing there, triumphant, holding the handgun. [2509] \"Aha,\" he said, \"I've finally found it.\" [2510] Chapter XXII: The Red Signal\n[2511] Sheriff Bartlett was standing in the library of Weinberg College. [2512] George Roxbury sat at a desk piled high with papers, frowning and looking haughty. [2513] Sheriff Bartlett briefly reported the situation, and the rest of the conversation was dominated by George, with the sheriff interjecting only occasionally with a word or two. [2514] On George's desk were the letters that Anthony had found on the dressing table. [2515] \"I don't understand,\" George said, snatching up the letter, \"you say these letters are written in code?\" [2516] \"Yes.\" [2517] \"And he found them on his dressing table?\" [2518] Chief Batter repeats Anthony's description word for word. [2519] \"So he handed them over to you right away? That's good, very good. But who would put these things in his room?\" [2520] Chief Batter shakes his head. [2521] \"You should know,\" George complained, \"this sounds suspicious, very suspicious. Anyway, what do we know about Kidd? His appearance is already strange, and in such a suspicious situation, we know nothing about him. Frankly, I don't like his act. Have you looked into his background?\" [2522] Bartlett remained patient, forcing a smile. [2523] \"We immediately sent a telegram to South Africa to confirm what he said. His time in Bulawayo with Mr. McGrath matches what he told us. He was working for the Joice Travels agency.\" [2524] \"Just as I suspected,\" George said, \"his brazen demeanor suits such a profession. But we need to act on these letters immediately. We can't afford to wait.\" [2525] The big man puffed himself up. [2526] \"Inspector Bately was about to speak when George interrupted, \"It's urgent. We must immediately decode these letters. I'm thinking of the person who knows all about the codes, the one related to the British Museum. He managed that department during the war. Miss Oscar should know. It's called...it's called...W...\"\n[2527] \"Wood Professor,\" Bately said. [2528] \"That's it! I remember now. I'll send him a telegram right away.\" [2529] \"Mr. Roxes, I sent a telegram an hour ago. He's booked for the 12:10 train.\" [2530] \"Ah, good, good.\n <Assistant> I have read the book and I will answer the question you ask.\n\nPassage 2:\nDialogue between User and Assistant 2026-06-12 03:45:22 \\n<User> The following context is the book I have read: \n[3140] \"Do you think someone is trying to play a trick on us?\u201d his father said nervously, \"I don't trust that Frenchman, L\u00e9on. The French police can pull off all sorts of tricks. They'll tie rubber bands around your arm, tell you the crime story, make you feel terrible, record your temperature with a thermometer, and then yell, 'Who killed the Prince of Michael?' My temperature might be 122 degrees or even more terrifying. Then they'll drag me straight to jail.\" [3141] The door opened, and Tredwell announced:\n[3142] \"Mr. George Romax, Mr. Everleigh.\" [3143] \"Cordes arrived, bringing his faithful hound,\" Bunder murmured. [3144] Bill walked directly to Bunder's side, while George greeted the Earl of Carringham with warmth, putting on his usual show in public. [3145] \"Dear Carringham,\" George said, shaking his hand, \"I came as soon as I received your message.\" [3146] \"You're too good, really. It's good to see you.\" [3147] The Duke of Carrington, always afraid of being impolite, unconsciously overdid his courtesy: \"It wasn't my message, but it doesn't matter.\" [3148] Meanwhile, Bill whispered to Bandel. [3149] \"What's going on? I heard Virginia ran off in the middle of the night. Did she get kidnapped?\" [3150] \"No,