y, she has other things to do now. She asked me to take good care of you, and I intend to, even if I have to use force.\" [1780] \"There's no need for force,\" Anthony comforted her, \"But if it's the same to you, I would prefer if you could entertain me on the lake, on a boat.\" [1781] \"That's a good idea,\" Bandel thought for a moment before answering. [1782] So they strolled over to the lakeside. [1783] \"Before we get to the main topic, I have one more question for you,\" Anthony said as he gently rowed the boat. \"Sweets after the bitter.\" [1784] \"Who's room are you going to inquire about this time?\" Bandel asked impatiently. [1785] \"This time, I'm not asking about a room. I want to know where you found your French tutor?\" [1786] \"You're out of your mind,\" Bunder said, \"I found her through an agency. I pay her a hundred pounds a year, her name is Jeanne Viel. What else do you want to know?\" [1787] \"Let's talk about the information the agency gave you,\" Anthony said, \"what's her background?\" [1788] \"Very impressive! She lived in the house of the Comtesse de Briodulle in Digne for ten years.\" [1789] \"Who is the Comtesse de Briodulle?\" [1790] \"The Comtesse de Briodulle, the Countess of Briodulle, is from the city of Digne, in France, at the Chateau de Briodulle.\" [1791] \"You haven't met the Countess, then? Corresponded by letter?\" [1792] \"Yes.\" [1793] \"Hmm?\" Anthony said. [1794] \"I'm confused, \" Bunder said. \"Very confused. Is this about a love affair or a murder investigation?\" [1795] \"Perhaps I'm just a fool. Let's not talk about it.\" [1796] \"No more.\" He said offhandedly, as he had gotten the information he wanted. [1797] \"Mr. Kidd, who do you suspect? I think the least likely is Virginia. Perhaps, maybe Bill?\" [1798] \"What do you think?\" [1799] \"A member of the nobility secretly joining the Red Hand would cause a sensation.\" [1800] Anthony laughed heartily. Although Bandler's piercing grey eyes gave him a bit of a fright