 room prepared for him to rest. Dinner was delivered to his room, and he did not meet anyone else in the villa, correct?\" [1184] \"Absolutely.\" [1185] \"This morning, a servant discovered the body at approximately 7:45. Dr. Carrington examined the body and found that he had been shot with a revolver. The gun was not found at the scene, and no one in the villa heard the gunshot. Furthermore, the victim's watch broke when he fell, indicating that the crime occurred at 11:45 p.m. Were you in bed at that time?\" [1186] \"I went to bed early. For some reason, last night's party was not very lively, and I'm sure you understand what I mean. We went upstairs around 10:30.\" [1187] \"Thank you. Lord Carrington, could you describe who else was staying in the house?\" [1188] \"I thought the killer had come from outside.\" [1189] The Chief Constable smiled. [1190] \"It should be, it should be. But I still need to know who was in the house.\" [1191] \"Sure, there's Prince Michael and his servant, and Mr. Herman Eschelbacher, the three of whom you already know. And there's Mr. Everly.\" [1192] \"He's an employee of my department.\" George modestly explained. [1193] \"Does he know Prince Michael's true purpose for coming here?\" [1194] \"No, I didn't tell him.\" George said seriously, \"He might feel something is wrong, but I don't need to confide in him.\" [1195] \"Understood. Lord Carrington, please continue.\" [1196] \"Let me think, there's Mr. Hiram Fisk.\" [1197] \"Who is Mr. Hiram Fisk?\" [1198] \"He's an American who brought a letter of introduction from Lucas Gott. Have you heard of Lucas Gott?\" [1199] Sheriff Bartlett smiled in agreement. Who hasn't heard of the name of the wealthy Lucas Gott? [1200] \"He's particularly interested in seeing my first edition collection. Lucas Gott's collection, of course, is unparalleled, but I also have some treasures. Mr. Fisk is also a fellow collector. Mr. Roamax suggested that I invite more people over the weekend to make this seem