usekeeper almost screamed when she saw him pass by.\" [3000] \"Well,\" Lemont said, \"I have to go. Sir, I just thought you should know the progress of the case.\" [3001] \"You are very considerate.\" The Earl of Carrington said, \"Would you like something to drink? Well, then goodnight!\" [3002] \"What a pest, with his little black mustache, glasses, and air of importance.\" As soon as he closed the door, Bander immediately said, \"I wish Anthony could straighten him out and make him angry! Virginia, what do you think?\" [3003] \"I don't know.\" Virginia said, \"I'm tired and want to go up to bed.\" [3004] \"Well, it's already eleven-thirty,\" The Earl of Carrington said. [3005] As Virginia walked through the spacious hall, she saw a broad back carefully leaving through the side door, and the figure felt familiar to her. [3006] \"Chief Inspector Batter!\" she called out eagerly. [3007] It was indeed him. Batter reluctantly retreated back into the room. [3008] \"Mrs. Rue, what's the matter?\" [3009] \"Mr. Lemon came by. He said Mr. Fisk is an American detective. Please tell me, is that true?\" [3010] Chief Inspector Batter nodded. [3011] \"Yes.\" [3012] \"You've known all along?\" [3013] Bartle Sheriff nodded again. [3014] Virginia turned towards the stairs. [3015] \"I see,\" she said. \"Thank you.\" [3016] Until this moment, she had not been willing to believe it was true. [3017] And now? [3018] She returned to her room and sat at her vanity, pondering the question. Every word Anthony had spoken took on new meaning, leaving her worried. [3019] Is this the \"deal\" he had mentioned? [3020] The \"deal\" he had given up on. But, what about later...\n[3021] An unusual sound disturbed her contemplation, causing her to look up in surprise. The time on her little gold watch read 1:30. She had been sitting there thinking for nearly two hours. [3022] The sound repeated, a tapping on the window glass. Virginia approached the window, opening it. A tall figure stood below in the alley, stooping down to pick up a handful of sand. [3023] Virginia's heart raced faster. Soon, she recognized the broad, muscular silhouette as that of Packard. [3024] \"I'm here,\" she whispered, \"What is it?\" [3025] It was strange for Packard to throw sand at her window at this hour. [3026] \"What is it?\" she asked impatiently. [3027] \"The master sent me,\" Boris's voice was low but clear. \"He sent me to fetch you.\" [3028] He spoke deliberately. [3029] \"To fetch me?\" [3030] \"Yes, he wants me to bring you to him. Here's a note, I'll toss it up to you.\" [3031] Virginia stepped back a little, and a note pressed down by a pebble fell at her feet. She opened the note, which read:\n[3032] Dear (Anthony wrote), I am in danger and am trying to escape. Will you believe me and come to me? [3033] Virginia stood there motionless for two minutes, reading and rereading the short message. [3034] She looked up, taking in the luxurious furnishings of the bedroom around her, feeling as if everything had changed. [3035] Then, she peered out the window again. [3036] \"What should I do?\" she asked. [3037] \"The detectives are on the other side of the villa, outside the conference room. You go downstairs and come out through the side door. I'll be waiting there, and I'll bring the car to the curb.\" [3038] Virginia nodded, quickly changing out of her dress and into a light yellow knit sweater, and donning a light yellow leather cap. [3039] She then wrote a short note, leaving it for Bunder, and pinned it to the needle cushion. [3040] She crept downstairs, unlocked the side door's latch. She hesitated for a moment, bravely tossing her head, much like her ancestors did when joining the Crusaders, and then stepped out. [3041] Chapter 26, October 13\n[3042] On October 13, Tuesday, at 10 a.m., Anthony Ked walked into the Hotel Harijgi to see Baron Lothrop Loyd, who was staying in a suite here. [3043] After an appropriate, aristocratic delay, Anthony was ushered into the baron's suite. The baron was standing upright on the rug by the fireplace, and so was Captain Andreas West, though with a slightly hostile air. [3044] As always, Anthony bowed deeply, touching his heels together, and performed the other formalities of the greeting ceremony. By now, he had become quite adept at it. [3045] \"I beg your pardon for coming so early, Baron,\" he said cheerfully as he placed his hat and cane on the table, \"but I have a business proposition I'd like to discuss with you.\" [3046] \"Really?\" the baron says. [3047] Captain Anastasia remains wary of Anthony, looking suspicious. [3048] \"Business,\" Anthony says. \"Based on the well-known principles of supply and demand. You need something, someone else has it, and the only thing left to discuss is the price.\" [3049] The baron studies him intently, saying nothing. [3050] \"An agreement should be easy to reach between a nobleman of Hesse-Schwarz and a British gentleman,\" Anthony continues. [3051] He spoke with a slight flush, as a British gentleman would not easily say such a thing. But he had seen the baron's great reaction to the statement before. Sure enough, the magic worked. [3052] \"Very good,\" said the baron, nodding approvingly. \"Quite right.\" [3053] Captain Anatole even softened his attitude somewhat, nodding along. [3054] \"Good,\" said Anthony. \"Then I'll get straight to the point.\" [3055] \"What? What did you say?\" interrupted the baron. \"Circuitous? I don't understand.\" [3056] \"Baron, that was just the preamble. In simpler terms, you need a cargo, we have cargo. This ship is fully equipped, but it's missing a captain. The 'ship' here refers to the Hessians, the royalists. Your political plan lacks a backbone, you've lost a prince! Now, hypothetically, let's say I can provide you with a prince. How about that?\" [3057] The baron's eyes widened. [3058] \"I don't understand at all,\" he said. [3059] \"Sir,\" Captain Androidsie growled, \"you're insulting us!\" [3060] \"Absolutely